    "created_at": "2016-08-08T21:27:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-08T21:27:41Z",
    "body": "There's nothing particularly weird about the Firefox behavior.  It just figures out the starting value by counting the number of LI children the OL has, while Chrome counts the number of LI _descendants_ not otherwise wrapped in a descendant list container.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
